    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d339">

                <pb facs="0406" n="390" sameAs="frus:frus1947v08/pg390"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">824.51/10–3147: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Flack</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">us urgent</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">La Paz</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-10-31T20:00:00-04:00">October 31, 1947—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>922. For Espy Assistant Chief NWC. See my US Urgent telegram No. 921
                        today.<anchor n="5" xml:id="d339-f1"/> On basis previous authorizations I
                    proceeded point where Bolivian Government made initial payment 2,500,000
                    bolivianos with promise additional equivalent $150,000 during month November. On
                    basis my negotiations Ernst had agreed deliver deed on payment initial 2,500,000
                    bolivianos. We now in receipt Department’s telegram 566 and Department’s airgram
                        242<anchor n="6" xml:id="d339-f2"/> requesting application this late date of
                    complicated procedure entirely unsuited conditions and situation Bolivia which
                    will have adverse effect on residence purchase unless it can be waived as
                    requested in my telegram cited. Please do everything possible enable Embassy
                    treat with this matter as contemplated section 3 Department’s telegram 408, July
                        11<anchor n="5" xml:id="d339-f3"/> and as envisaged my negotiations to date.
                    Am departing November 4 but Galbraith fully informed.<anchor n="7"
                        xml:id="d339-f4"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Flack</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
